{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative","id":1318553,"title":"Isn't there any Rote for gaining initiative?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-14T15:36:50-07:00","id":1318553,"title":"Isn't there any Rote for gaining initiative?","content":"I mean, every creature in the WoD has it's ways of getting a better initiative, werewolves have their &quot;broken&quot; <i>Spirit of the Fray</i> gift, vampires have celerity, can enhance their dex and the Tremere have <i>Path of Focused Mind</i> and some rituals that can be used to boost initiative, but I'm yet to come across a single mage route to boost initiative. Why is that so? Should mages be slow? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T15:52:55-07:00","id":1318557,"title":"","content":"I feel like I've seen one before, but I couldn't tell you where. Still, using Mind to enhance Wits or Life to improve your Dexterity would do effectively the same thing, and could easily be coincidental. Otherwise, Time ought to help, perhaps even at Rank 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25373-athanasius-digges","name":"Athanasius Digges","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T16:03:18-07:00","id":1318561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Athanasius Digges</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1318557#post1318557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I've seen one before, but I couldn't tell you where. Still, using Mind to enhance Wits or Life to improve your Dexterity would do effectively the same thing, and could easily be coincidental. Otherwise, Time ought to help, perhaps even at Rank 1.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Still it would be hardly ever enough to get initiative against werewolves and vampires for instance. A rote for that would be really welcomed. If stupid werewolves can get 10 plus 10 extra initiative with only a level 2 gift (and 1 gnosis point for the extra 10), mages should have something AT THE VERY LEAST on the same level as their magic allow them to both deal with spirits, enhance their minds, control time, and everything. It's hard to believe they left this huge gap...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T17:20:10-07:00","id":1318564,"title":"","content":"There are many ways to actually accomplish this. Just because there is no written Rote doesn't mean you can't think up a spell for something. That's the whole point of Mage's magic system, isn't it?<br /> <br /> However, the character would have to cast that spell in advance (or maybe wear wonder with a passive +initiative effect) to really profit from this, or else they would waste at least the first turn of combat by casting something that could give them the edge in speed. Also, just because a gift exists that enhances initiative for werewolves, doesn't mean it's a benchmark for that splat! SOME werewolves may be this fast but there are many other level 2 gifts that are also useful, not only in combat situations, to choose from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T17:53:11-07:00","id":1318570,"title":"","content":"Any Werewolf worth his salt has it, in any case werewolves live for combat. I know the Mage's magic system is for that, but there are usually guidelines for most kind of effects, yet not any for initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T18:28:13-07:00","id":1318575,"title":"","content":"Time and Mind or Time and Life. would be my go tos. &quot;I go first&quot; Since you can litterally see the future and plan accordingly. I'd probably make it 2 and 2. Hell I might just let someone do it with Time 2. Better Body would be your other option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T18:36:48-07:00","id":1318582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1318575#post1318575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time and Mind or Time and Life. would be my go tos. &quot;I go first&quot; Since you can litterally see the future and plan accordingly. I'd probably make it 2 and 2. Hell I might just let someone do it with Time 2. Better Body would be your other option.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see, but the point is that there are no system, no example of any system regarding it and of course I can come up with one, but I think it's very strange that there aren't ANY rote for that. Better body would really suck compared to what werewolves and vampires can make...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T19:04:21-07:00","id":1318584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1318582#post1318582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I see, but the point is that there are no system, no example of any system regarding it and of course I can come up with one, but I think it's very strange that there aren't ANY rote for that. Better body would really suck compared to what werewolves and vampires can make...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is extremely open ended. The issue Is that Innitiatlve is.. WEIRD. IT functions outside any other system. You'll notice how generally mage effects are fairly BROAD use.. while werewolf ones are extremely narrow(But they get so many gift options)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T23:06:54-07:00","id":1318612,"title":"","content":"Time-Motion Study<br /> <br /> Technocracy: Iteration X page 49 <br /> Correspondence 1, Time 1 <br /> <br /> This Procedure allows an Iterator to analyze their movements and determine the most efficient way to accomplish a task. It gives a bonus of one per success of their next initiative roll.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that this can be done with just Life 1, maybe Mind 1, Time 1. Possibly any sphere lvl 1...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T23:56:33-07:00","id":1318618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1318612#post1318612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time-Motion Study<br /> <br /> Technocracy: Iteration X page 49<br /> Correspondence 1, Time 1<br /> <br /> This Procedure allows an Iterator to analyze their movements and determine the most efficient way to accomplish a task. It gives a bonus of one per success of their next initiative roll.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that this can be done with just Life 1, maybe Mind 1, Time 1. Possibly any sphere lvl 1...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's interesting, but a Tremere can accomplish the same with <i>The Path of Focused Mind </i>1, rolling against a difficulty of 4 with their Willpower as dice pool. I think it's nice to know that there's at least one rote for such an important thing like initiative in the WoD. Still I think it falls short of what <i>Spirit of the Fray</i> alone does. As I see probably there are not any other rote for initiative in Mage and it's disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T07:18:28-07:00","id":1318672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1318618#post1318618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's interesting, but a Tremere can accomplish the same with <i>The Path of Focused Mind </i>1, rolling against a difficulty of 4 with their Willpower as dice pool. I think it's nice to know that there's at least one rote for such an important thing like initiative in the WoD. Still I think it falls short of what <i>Spirit of the Fray</i> alone does. As I see probably there are not any other rote for initiative in Mage and it's disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>A coincidental lvl 1 spell will have difficulty of 4 too. It would be the same as the Path of Focused Mind.<br /> What does the gift do? I think the rote is pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T07:28:38-07:00","id":1318674,"title":"","content":"As noted, Spirit of the Fray permanently increases your Initiative by 10, and you can further increase it for a turn at the rate of 10 per point of Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Of course, most people consider it badly written at best because it's such a massive increase. Nobody have anything matching that, so comparing any rote to it is futile.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T07:58:09-07:00","id":1318680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1318618#post1318618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting, but a Tremere can accomplish the same with <i>The Path of Focused Mind </i>1, rolling against a difficulty of 4 with their Willpower as dice pool. I think it's nice to know that there's at least one rote for such an important thing like initiative in the WoD. Still I think it falls short of what <i>Spirit of the Fray</i> alone does. As I see probably there are not any other rote for initiative in Mage and it's disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you that the wrote was written in a 1st Edition book - which started off with mages dropping instruments left and right and having higher Arete ratings on average than they do these days.<br /> <br /> The rote might need a subtle reivison, perhaps scaling the initiative increase more with the Damage Table of Arete successes (So, roughly 2x successes). Else it's rather underwhelming.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a similiar note, if you really want to boost your initiative, have a Time 2/Mind 1 effect running that essentially simply allows you to see about..one second into the future. Just one second is all it takes. Not only is that very short of a future sense rather accurate, but the initiative gain is probably...impressive as hell. The rote could also take additional successes to be spent into dodge difficulty decrease and even to-hit difficulty decrease.<br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 06-17-2019, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T08:13:48-07:00","id":1318686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1318674#post1318674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As noted, Spirit of the Fray permanently increases your Initiative by 10, and you can further increase it for a turn at the rate of 10 per point of Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Of course, most people consider it badly written at best because it's such a massive increase. Nobody have anything matching that, so comparing any rote to it is futile.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course Mage isn't built along the idea that someone is going to have a blanket buff but rather what's available by spheres and spheres alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T02:06:11-07:00","id":1318817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1318570#post1318570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Werewolf worth his salt has it, in any case werewolves live for combat. I know the Mage's magic system is for that, but there are usually guidelines for most kind of effects, yet not any for initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the first misconception. Sure, werewolves are made to fight but the game is actually about why always fighting is a bad idea. Just because one gift is powerful in certain situations not everyone will have to take it. Werewolves are good fighters regardless of this single gift.<br /> The second misconception is that you want to compare splats. Werewolves ARE made to fight and mages are not. You can use that Rote (Procedure) described above in the thread but that's just a reaction to a situation, so it probably must be fast-cast anyways. A mage could cast a lingering &quot;fast reflexes&quot; or &quot;fast reaction&quot; spell on herself but even that could never compare to a flat, passive +10 initiative and it should never do that! Vampires and Changelings also don't have a counter for this and why would they?<br /> <br /> I can understand your question about how a mage could possibly increase her initiative but everything else is rather... power gamey. And I'm very sorry if that feels a bit bad but I'm totally against just setting a benchmark for a splat, what spells/gifts/disciplines they should always take. The benchmark is the splat itself, everything else is personality!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T09:16:47-07:00","id":1318877,"title":"","content":"I agree to a successes x2 bonus initiative. Also, as posted, not all garou will have the gift. And having high initiative (acting first) isn't all that powerful...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T10:01:21-07:00","id":1318882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1318817#post1318817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's the first misconception. Sure, werewolves are made to fight but the game is actually about why always fighting is a bad idea. Just because one gift is powerful in certain situations not everyone will have to take it. Werewolves are good fighters regardless of this single gift.<br /> The second misconception is that you want to compare splats. Werewolves ARE made to fight and mages are not. You can use that Rote (Procedure) described above in the thread but that's just a reaction to a situation, so it probably must be fast-cast anyways. A mage could cast a lingering &quot;fast reflexes&quot; or &quot;fast reaction&quot; spell on herself but even that could never compare to a flat, passive +10 initiative and it should never do that! Vampires and Changelings also don't have a counter for this and why would they?<br /> <br /> I can understand your question about how a mage could possibly increase her initiative but everything else is rather... power gamey. And I'm very sorry if that feels a bit bad but I'm totally against just setting a benchmark for a splat, what spells/gifts/disciplines they should always take. The benchmark is the splat itself, everything else is personality!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Changelings cheat by having Triggers.. like &quot;getting into combat&quot; which beats intitiative boosters(which they have.. but are not super impressive +1 per success.. Plus +3 per 2(Because each 2nd success give a dex buff) Of course.. mages also have that cheat too in Time 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T04:16:42-07:00","id":1319027,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to say that Spirit of the Frey isn't overpowered but you have to remember that in order to get those extra 10 on initiative (above the extra 10 you get from learning the gift) you have to spend Gnosis, which means that you won't be able to spend Rage in that turn. And since it's a gift for Ahrouns only, who regularly use Rage to fuel their other gifts or even to buy themselves extra actions it won't be high on the priority list on stuff to activate on the first round of combat, or even 2nd round for that matter.<br /> <br /> Though I would probably house rule it so that you roll Gnosis to activate it and each success adds to your Initiative. Then you can spend a Gnosis to add another 10 to that result.<br /> <br /> <br /> But to get back to the topic at hand, I can see a rote where you use Time 2/Life 1/Mind 1. Each success adds 2 to your Initiative rating for the next turn (or you can choose to spend some of the successes to increase the duration rather than bonus to Initiative).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T09:09:58-07:00","id":1319066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1319027#post1319027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to say that Spirit of the Frey isn't overpowered but you have to remember that in order to get those extra 10 on initiative (above the extra 10 you get from learning the gift) you have to spend Gnosis, which means that you won't be able to spend Rage in that turn. And since it's a gift for Ahrouns only, who regularly use Rage to fuel their other gifts or even to buy themselves extra actions it won't be high on the priority list on stuff to activate on the first round of combat, or even 2nd round for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 10+ by itself is pretty insane. Assuming at least a 3 and 3 that means they have 16 before a die is even rolled. Hell if it gave +5 it would still be insane.. Maybe if it cost Gnosis or rage to use.. but it doesn't unless you are fighting someone else who has it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T10:44:19-07:00","id":1319081,"title":"","content":"Arete successes x2 is a lot too. Using a lvl 1 sphere is dif 4. An initial mage could get +6.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1319027#post1319027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But to get back to the topic at hand, I can see a rote where you use Time 2/Life 1/Mind 1. Each success adds 2 to your Initiative rating for the next turn (or you can choose to spend some of the successes to increase the duration rather than bonus to Initiative).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're not using the dividing successes rule, then 3 successes would give +6 for a whole day already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T05:38:08-07:00","id":1319257,"title":"","content":"Yep. It's indeed good.<br /> <br /> And one needs to remember how Magick works when compared with Gifts and Disciplines. Persistent effects nearly always imply Rituals in Mage, they're not something that you do willy nilly.<br /> <br /> As Ritual under M20 rules w/o dividing succersses and using successes x2, you can overpower Spirit of the Fray in 10 successes (+20 Inititative w/o expending shit with a duration so massive it may well be permanent. Revised had a penalty of +1 to your rolls per each 2 persistent effects, but under M20 you can avoid this). Under the optional rules of Rite, Ceremony and Great Work that's a Ceremony (1 roll per hour, max five rolls. At diff 4, a Disiciple shouldn't have a lot of problems to get there). If you opt for the +1 per success you would need a Great Work that may require several days to do the same, but it's still doable. And if we're already doing a Great Work, adding permanency isn't out of the question<br /> <br /> If needing so much prep sounds unfair...think on how much time, effort and resources the werewolf spent to get the Gift &quot;casted&quot; upon them. That's a seeking in the Umbra, Chriminage and xp you're expending. It also takes time, and it costs a lot more if the ST doesn't limit the power somehow (I.E. Invoking some form of Paradox after a certain threshold).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-18-2019, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T05:49:22-07:00","id":1319260,"title":"","content":"And you should always be working hard to get those Difficulty breaks, so there's no reason the Difficulty can't be as low as you can get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T10:49:53-07:00","id":1319756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1319257#post1319257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. It's indeed good.<br /> <br /> And one needs to remember how Magick works when compared with Gifts and Disciplines. Persistent effects nearly always imply Rituals in Mage, they're not something that you do willy nilly.<br /> <br /> As Ritual under M20 rules w/o dividing succersses and using successes x2, you can overpower Spirit of the Fray in 10 successes (+20 Inititative w/o expending shit with a duration so massive it may well be permanent. Revised had a penalty of +1 to your rolls per each 2 persistent effects, but under M20 you can avoid this). Under the optional rules of Rite, Ceremony and Great Work that's a Ceremony (1 roll per hour, max five rolls. At diff 4, a Disiciple shouldn't have a lot of problems to get there). If you opt for the +1 per success you would need a Great Work that may require several days to do the same, but it's still doable. And if we're already doing a Great Work, adding permanency isn't out of the question<br /> <br /> If needing so much prep sounds unfair...think on how much time, effort and resources the werewolf spent to get the Gift &amp;quot;casted&amp;quot; upon them. That's a seeking in the Umbra, Chriminage and xp you're expending. It also takes time, and it costs a lot more if the ST doesn't limit the power somehow (I.E. Invoking some form of Paradox after a certain threshold).</div> </div> </div> </div>It was only a persistent effect if you didn't give it a duration. Once you spent successes to give It a duration it was no longer persistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T12:28:14-07:00","id":1319985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1318553-isn-t-there-any-rote-for-gaining-initiative?p=1319257#post1319257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. It's indeed good.<br /> <br /> And one needs to remember how Magick works when compared with Gifts and Disciplines. Persistent effects nearly always imply Rituals in Mage, they're not something that you do willy nilly.<br /> <br /> As Ritual under M20 rules w/o dividing succersses and using successes x2, you can overpower Spirit of the Fray in 10 successes (+20 Inititative w/o expending shit with a duration so massive it may well be permanent. Revised had a penalty of +1 to your rolls per each 2 persistent effects, but under M20 you can avoid this). Under the optional rules of Rite, Ceremony and Great Work that's a Ceremony (1 roll per hour, max five rolls. At diff 4, a Disiciple shouldn't have a lot of problems to get there). If you opt for the +1 per success you would need a Great Work that may require several days to do the same, but it's still doable. And if we're already doing a Great Work, adding permanency isn't out of the question<br /> <br /> If needing so much prep sounds unfair...think on how much time, effort and resources the werewolf spent to get the Gift &quot;casted&quot; upon them. That's a seeking in the Umbra, Chriminage and xp you're expending. It also takes time, and it costs a lot more if the ST doesn't limit the power somehow (I.E. Invoking some form of Paradox after a certain threshold).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This option seems good enough. It gives a mage the chance to beat werewolves and vampires in initiative if they are prepared enough, though with permanency it would be a little unfair lol. But as a ritual you go when preparing for &quot;stressful&quot; situations it's seems good and balanced enough. Thank you again Aleph and everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}